666220232,2026-10-10 11:55:24,calmwater2000,2017-12-19,221,2,,"$SMCI Sun’s sentencing is set for September 8, 2027. His October 8, 2026 guilty plea could accelerate prosecution of the remaining defendants, especially if he cooperates. The key question now is whether Sun will testify against SMCI co-founder Wally Liaw. Supermicro’s August 20 independent investigation, conducted with outside counsel and forensic accountants, found: - No evidence current senior management knew about the alleged diversion scheme. - No evidence of direct sales to known restricted customers or locations. - No evidence the alleged diversion compromised prior financial statements. - Additional compliance improvements were needed, which the board accepted. These findings support a favorable scenario in which criminal liability remains limited to individuals rather than extending to SMCI. If court proceedings reinforce these findings, a major legal overhang on SMCI&#39;s valuation could lift."
