666665732,2026-10-16 02:41:01,Kemojoe7,2026-06-12,0,0,Bearish,"$SMCI I believe in what this company could do, but the leadership and oversight concerns are hard to ignore. This goes beyond rumors. Contractor Willy Sun pleaded guilty in the China server-export case. Co-founder Wally Liaw and a Taiwan manager were also charged, although charges aren’t convictions. Supermicro itself wasn’t named as a defendant in that indictment. Then there’s the company’s $17.5 million SEC accounting settlement from 2020. Sara Liu also sold about $4.5 million in shares on October 7 under a previously established trading plan. That alone doesn’t prove anything, but it doesn’t build my confidence either. Why sell if you believe in the company that you are connected to? My question is simple: what has changed in the oversight and operations to keep these problems from happening again? The worry is that the problem could be systemic. The technology matters, but so do the operations and people running the company."
